#: ../../solid/cell_transformations.rst:2
msgid "単位胞と座標系の変換"
msgstr "Unit Cell and Coordinate System Transformations"

#: ../../solid/cell_transformations.rst:4
msgid ""
"同じ結晶でも、基本単位胞と慣用単位胞、超胞、座標軸の向き、原点の取り方によって、格子ベクトルや 原子座標の数値は変わります。\\ "
":ref:`格子基底と座標系の変換<lattice-transform>`\\ で変換則を導き、 "
"FCCで単位胞を取り直して原子位置や指数の変わり方を確かめ、六方・菱面体などの格子で胞の形だけではブラベー格子型が決まらないことを見ます。続いて、ペロブスカイトの擬立方格子を見ます。"
" 最後に、構造の標準化と計算ソフトへの入力に当てはめます。"
msgstr ""
"Even for the same crystal, the numerical values of the lattice vectors "
"and atomic coordinates depend on whether we use a primitive cell, "
"conventional cell, or supercell, which axes we choose, and where we place"
" the origin. In \\ :ref:`Lattice Basis and Coordinate System "
"Transformations <lattice-transform>`\\ , we derive the transformation "
"rules. We then use FCC to see how atomic positions and indices change "
"when we choose a new unit cell, and use hexagonal and rhombohedral "
"examples to show why the cell shape alone does not determine the Bravais "
"lattice type. Next we look at the pseudocubic lattice of a perovskite. "
"Finally, we apply these ideas to structure standardization and input for "
"calculation software."

